<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malaya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malaya was the name for British territories on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, comprising the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straits-settlements">Straits Settlements</a> and the Malay states under British protection. It was valued for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s rapid conquest of Malaya and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> in 1941 to 1942 dealt a severe blow to the prestige of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>, and Malaya became independent in 1957.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…extensive economic system the world had yet seen, linking the agricultural resources of India, the plantation economies of the Caribbean and later West Africa and <b>Malaya</b>, the mineral wealth of Australia and South Africa, and the manufacturing output of industrial Britain within a sterling-based trading and monetary system.</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Australia fought in Korea, <b>Malaya</b> and Vietnam, where national servicemen served from 1966, led the international force in East Timor in 1999 and joined the wars in Afghanistan and Iraq.</blockquote><a href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia">Commonwealth of Australia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Johor accepted a British adviser in 1914, joined the Federation of <b>Malaya</b> in 1948, which became independent in 1957, and became a state of Malaysia in 1963.</blockquote><a href="/empire/johor-sultanate">Johor Sultanate · Into the Present</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Second World War, Malay opposition defeated the British plan for a centralised Malayan Union, and the Federation of <b>Malaya</b> was created in 1948, while a communist insurgency, the Malayan Emergency, was fought from 1948 to 1960.</blockquote><a href="/empire/malaysia">Malaysia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>This was owed partly to its position as a buffer between British Burma and <b>Malaya</b> on one side and French Indochina on the other, and partly to the diplomacy of Mongkut and Chulalongkorn and their timely concessions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/rattanakosin-kingdom">Rattanakosin Kingdom · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Its forces fought in Korea, in colonial conflicts in <b>Malaya</b>, Kenya and Cyprus, at Suez in 1956 and in the Falklands War of 1982, and were deployed in Northern Ireland from 1969 to 2007.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom · Military</a></li></ul></section>
